GeanyVosk — Voice Control Plugin for Geany
==========================================

Offline voice control for the Geany IDE using the Vosk speech recognition
library and ALSA audio capture.

Wake phrase : "Rub lamp"   (activates command mode)
Deactivate  : "Back in the lamp"

Dependencies
------------
  libvosk        — https://alphacephei.com/vosk/models (C library + vosk_api.h)
  libasound2-dev — ALSA audio capture (routes through PulseAudio via "pulse" device)

Model Setup
-----------
Download a Vosk model from https://alphacephei.com/vosk/models and extract it to:
  ~/.local/share/geanyvosk/model/

The small English model (~40 MB) is recommended for command use:
  unzip vosk-model-small-en-us-0.22.zip
  mv vosk-model-small-en-us-0.22 ~/.local/share/geanyvosk/model

Verify the layout is correct:
  ~/.local/share/geanyvosk/model/am/final.mdl

Configuration
-------------
Optional config file: ~/.config/geany/geanyvosk.conf

  [geanyvosk]

  # Path to the Vosk model directory (default: ~/.local/share/geanyvosk/model)
  # Leave commented to use the default; the path must be absolute (no ~ expansion).
  #model_path=/home/youruser/.local/share/geanyvosk/model

  # ALSA capture device (default: pulse — routes through PulseAudio)
  # Use "pulse" to honour the microphone selected in Ubuntu Sound Settings,
  # including Bluetooth headsets.
  # To target a specific device, use its PulseAudio source name, e.g.:
  #   alsa_device=bluez_source.24_B2_31_93_F1_93.handsfree_head_unit
  # List available sources with: pactl list sources short
  alsa_device=pulse

  # Phrase that activates command mode (default: rub lamp)
  wake_word=rub lamp

  # Phrase that deactivates command mode (default: back in the lamp)
  deactivate_word=back in the lamp

Voice Commands
--------------
Once active (after saying the wake phrase), the following commands are recognised:

  UI control (requires GeanyControl plugin):
    "switch to agent"           — focus the Agent tab in the message window
    "switch to cli"             — focus the CLI tab
    "save all"                  — save all open documents
    "close file"                — close the current file
    "refresh"                   — emit geanycontrol-refresh signal

  File creation: 
    "agent create new skill <name>"   — create ~/.claude/skills/<name>.md from
                                        template and open it in the editor
    "new ai prompt <name> dot md"     — create ./ai-prompts/<name>.md and open it

  Menu navigation:
    "menu <name>"               — open a top-level menu by name (e.g. "menu file",
                                  "menu edit", "menu build")
                                  Status bar shows "menu". The first item is
                                  pre-selected.
    "<item name>"               — highlight the item whose label contains the spoken
                                  text (case-insensitive substring match)
    "up" / "up <N>"             — move selection up one or N items
    "down" / "down <N>"         — move selection down one or N items
    "go"                        — activate the highlighted item
    "back in the lamp" / "cancel" — close the menu without activating anything

    Example:
      "menu file"       → opens File menu, first item selected
      "save all"        → highlights "Save All" item
      "go"              → executes it

  Tree browser control (requires TreeBrowser + GeanyControl plugins):
    "sidebar"                   — enter tree navigation mode.  Status bar shows
                                  "tree" (green).  The TreeBrowser sidebar panel
                                  is focused automatically.
    "up" / "up <N>"             — move cursor up N rows in the file tree
    "down" / "down <N>"         — move cursor down N rows
    "go" / "open"               — open selected file or expand/collapse directory
    "refresh"                   — refresh the current directory listing
    "home"                      — navigate to home directory (~/)
    "project root"              — navigate to the open project's base path
    "set path"                  — set tree root to the current document's directory
    "menu"                      — show context menu for the selected item; then
                                  navigate it with "up"/"down"/"<item name>"/"go"
    "back in the lamp" / "cancel" — exit tree browser mode

    Example:
      "sidebar"        → focus tree panel, status = "tree"
      "down three"     → move cursor down 3 rows
      "go"             → open the selected file
      "menu"           → show right-click menu, status = "menu"
      "delete"         → highlight Delete item
      "go"             → execute it

  Dictation:
    "dictate"                   — enter dictation mode; subsequent speech is appended as text to the current document
    "stop dictating"            — return to command mode

    While dictating, the following spoken phrases are converted to punctuation
    or formatting instead of being inserted literally:

      "full stop"         → .
      "comma"             → ,
      "question mark"     → ?
      "exclamation mark"  → !
      "colon"             → :
      "semicolon"         → ;
      "open bracket"      → (
      "close bracket"     → )
      "new line"          → newline character
      "new paragraph"     → two newlines
      "start list"        → newline + "- "
      "list item"         → newline + "- "
      "tab"               → tab character

  Agent skill execution (requires GeanyAgent + GeanyControl):
    "agent skill <model> <verb> [context <file> dot md]"
                                — arm a skill command (status bar shows
                                  "Skill armed — say Go")
    "go"                        — execute the armed skill in the agent terminal

    model values : opus, sonnet, haiku
    verb values  : plan, exec

    Example:
      "agent skill opus plan context my project dot md"
      "go"
      → sends: /opus-plan @ai-prompts/my-project.md

Status Bar Indicator
--------------------
When the plugin loads, a microphone icon and short label appear at the right end
of Geany's status bar.  The label and icon opacity tell you the current state:

  idle       — plugin loaded, audio capture running, Vosk listening for the wake
               word.  Icon pulses faintly (opacity alternates ~0.2 / ~0.5).
               This is what you should see on startup.

  listening  — wake word recognised ("rub lamp"), command mode active.
               Icon brightens and pulses green.  Say a command now.

  dictating  — dictation mode active.  Icon solid orange.  Speech is appended
               directly to the current document.

  agent      — composing text for the agent input field.

  say go!    — a skill command is armed and waiting for confirmation.
               Icon pulses yellow.  Say "go" to execute or "back in the lamp" to
               cancel.

  menu       — a menu bar entry is open and waiting for navigation.
               Icon solid purple.  Say an item name, "up", "down", "go", or
               "cancel".

  tree       — TreeBrowser navigation mode active.  Icon solid green.  Voice
               commands navigate the file tree.

  off        — voice commands disabled via Tools → Voice Commands toggle.
               Icon dim grey, no blinking.

Expected startup sequence
-------------------------
1. Load/enable the plugin.
2. Status bar shows "idle" with a faintly blinking microphone icon.
3. Say "rub lamp" — label changes to "listening" and icon turns green.
4. Say a command (e.g. "save all").
5. Say "back in the lamp" — label returns to "idle".

If the label stays "idle" and never changes to "listening" after saying
"rub lamp", see Troubleshooting below.

Troubleshooting
---------------
Icon not visible
  The icon and label are appended to the Geany progress-bar row.  If the status
  bar is hidden (View → Show Status Bar) the widgets will not appear.

Wake word not recognised — "idle" never changes to "listening"
  While idle the recogniser is constrained to the wake phrase (a Vosk phrase
  grammar) so it is caught reliably; once active it switches to the full
  vocabulary for commands and dictation.  This requires a lookahead model
  (the recommended vosk-model-small-en-us is one); precompiled HCLG graph
  models do not support grammar and the wake word will be hard to recognise.

  1. Check that the plugin was compiled with Vosk support:
       grep -r HAVE_VOSK geanyvosk/src/.deps/
     If HAVE_VOSK is absent, speech recognition is compiled out.  Reinstall
     libvosk development headers and rebuild.

  2. Verify the model path is correct:
       ls ~/.local/share/geanyvosk/model/am/final.mdl
     If missing, see Model Setup above.

  3. Confirm audio is reaching the plugin.  Rebuild with -DVOSK_DUMP_PCM (see
     Debugging Audio below) and play back the captured audio.

  4. Check Geany's status bar (bottom of window) for "GeanyVosk:" messages on
     load — model errors are reported there.

Debugging Audio
---------------
To verify microphone capture, rebuild with -DVOSK_DUMP_PCM.  Raw audio is
written to /tmp/geanyvosk.raw while the plugin is loaded.  Play it back with:
  aplay -f S16_LE -r 16000 -c 1 /tmp/geanyvosk.raw
